      "text": "The goal isn’t to create MORE digital products.\nIt’s to create something that solves a problem people are already willing to pay to solve.\nHere are 7 simple ideas I’d consider:\n✨ 1. Templates\nCanva templates, social media templates, resumes, invitations, media kits, or business templates.\n✨ 2. Mini guides\nA short, actionable guide that helps someone get one specific result.\n✨ 3. Prompt packs\nReady-to-use ChatGPT prompts for content, business, productivity, job searching, or a specific niche.\n✨ 4. Planners\nBudget planners, meal planners, content planners, fitness planners, or business planners.\n✨ 5. Trackers\nHabit trackers, savings trackers, income trackers, content trackers, or goal trackers.\n✨ 6. Checklists\nStep-by-step checklists that make a confusing process easier to follow.\n✨ 7. Workbooks\nInteractive PDFs that walk someone through a specific problem or goal.\nThe key?\nDon’t start by asking:\n“What should I create?”\nStart by asking:\n“What problem is my audience actively trying to solve?”\nThen build the simplest product that helps them solve it. ⚡\nYou don’t need 20 products.\nYou need one useful product + the right audience + content that makes them want the solution.\n\\ud83d\\udcab Comment BLUEPRINT and I’ll send you my guide to starting a faceless digital product business.\nMake sure you follow. #digitalmarketing #webmarketing #marketingjobs #careerchange #skillup",
